    "lastText": "The spreadsheet engine is built and every item in TASK.md is implemented. `npm test` runs 64 tests and all pass.\n\nThe repo contained only TASK.md, so I created everything:\n\n- **`src/sheet.js`**: the `Sheet` class (exported as both `module.exports` and `.Sheet`). It has a tokenizer, a precedence-climbing parser, and an evaluator. Cycles are found with a topological pass, so cells in a cycle, and cells that reach one, show `#CIRC!` without being evaluated. This also avoids deep recursion on long chains.\n- **`test/sheet.test.js`**: covers the API, literals, operators, coercion, errors, cycles, every function group, and a 3000-cell chain and sheet-wide ranges at the `ZZ9999` limit.\n- **`package.json`**: `\"test\": \"node --test\"`, no dependencies.\n- **`README.md`**: the API, the language rules, and every supported function.\n\nI have not committed anything, since you did not ask for a commit.\n\nJudgment calls where TASK.md was silent or ambiguous:\n\n- **Static cycle detection:** a reference inside an unused `IF` branch still counts as a dependency, so `=IF(FALSE, A1, 1)` in `A1` is `#CIRC!`.\n- **Errors in ranges:** errors inside a range propagate through aggregates such as `SUM`, `COUNT` and `AVERAGE`. `COUNTA` counts them as non-empty.\n- **`COUNT`:** scalar arguments count if they coerce to a number, and non-numeric text is not counted rather than raising an error.\n- **Comparisons with empty cells:** an empty cell compares as `FALSE` against booleans.\n- **Criteria:** a numeric-looking criterion such as `\"5\"` matches only numeric cells. `COUNTIF` with `\"<>x\"` does not count empty cells.\n- **Lookups:** error cells are skipped during matching, and a lookup result that is an error still propagates.\n- **`MATCH`:** a two-dimensional range gives `#VALUE!`.\n- **`ROUND`:** it works on the decimal string form, so `ROUND(2.675, 2)` gives 2.68.\n- **Performance:** any read after a write recomputes the whole sheet. That is simple and correct, but a loop that alternates writes and reads on a very large sheet will be slow.",
